First Author: Weigt
Title: Development and validation of a bronchoalveolar lavage genomic classifier for acute cellular rejection
Source number: 72

Very short summary: This prospective multicenter cohort study analysed 806 bronchoalveolar-lavage cell-pellet RNA-sequencing samples from 181 lung transplant recipients in CTOT-20, with independent validation using a UCLA cohort. A 31-gene Random Forest classifier distinguished clinically significant acute cellular rejection from stable controls; in the independent validation subset, it achieved an AUC of 0.90 (95% CI 0.83–0.96), accuracy of 82.1%, sensitivity of 73.3%, and specificity of 87.5%.

