	•	Section 1 Comments/Quotes: CTOT-20 was a prospective observational cohort enrolling adult lung transplant recipients at five North American centres: Duke University, UCLA, University of Toronto, Johns Hopkins, and Cleveland Clinic. Participants were transplanted between December 2015 and August 2018; the consecutively sampled study subset was transplanted from August 2016 to April 2017, with follow-up through July 2021. Funding included National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases awards, with additional Cystic Fibrosis Foundation and Saul and Joyce Brandman Foundation support. Multiple author conflicts were declared, including research grants, consulting, honoraria, advisory roles, and a provisional patent related to allograft injury or rejection.

